-- title:
--   Existence of a Drinfeld basis after a finite base change
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$, and $W_0$ a complete discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$; let $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal. Let $F_0$ be a commutative formal group law over $k$ satisfying `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic` for the ideal $\bot$, the integer $q$ and parameters $0,0$, i.e. $F_0$'s $q$-series equals a unit power series times `F₀.drinfeldDivisor q 0 0`; and let $F_u$ be a commutative formal group law over the power series ring $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$ whose defining series maps coefficientwise, under $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$, to that of $F_0$. Then there exists a type $V$ carrying a commutative ring structure which is a domain, is local, is a $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$-algebra, and is complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, such that the structure map $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket \to V$ is injective, and there is a formal group law $G$ over $V$ whose series is the coefficientwise image of that of $F_u$, together with $\alpha, \beta$ in the maximal ideal of $V$ with `G.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic (maximalIdeal V) q α β`.
--
--   This is the splitting step for Drinfeld level structures on the universal (Lubin–Tate) deformation: the $q$-division series of the universal formal group acquires a full set of $q^2$ distinct roots in the maximal ideal after passage to a complete local domain dominating $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$. It feeds the injectivity statement [`FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.injective_algebraMap_of_represents_isDrinfeldBasisAdic`](thm.html#FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.injective_algebraMap_of_represents_isDrinfeldBasisAdic) for the Lubin–Tate coordinate on the deformation ring with Drinfeld level structure.
